Hi Alex, and the Partner Technology team,

Thank you again for taking Pontardawe RFC's online checkout live. We are now =
launching Vesopa EPOS to new venues, and we want them to pay for their subscr=
iption with Dojo too.

We have built this on the Dojo sandbox. Please could you certify the integrat=
ion and give Vesopa Software Ltd access to the live online payments API?

ALREADY LIVE WITH DOJO
- Card machines: Vesopa EPOS drives Dojo card machines from the till: sales, =
refunds, tips, split bills and cashback. Accredited with you in October.
- Online checkout: Pontardawe RFC's online menu (menu.pontardawerfc.com) pass=
ed your online checkout review on 20 October and is live on Dojo.

WHAT WE HAVE BUILT ON THE SANDBOX
1. Sign-up and trial: a venue picks a plan on vesopaepos.com/trial. A =C2=A31=
 payment on Dojo's hosted checkout confirms the card, Apple Pay or Google Pay=
, and is refunded through the API straight away. A 14-day free trial then sta=
rts.
2. First charge and renewals: a payment intent per invoice, paid on Dojo's ho=
sted checkout (pay.dojo.tech) from an emailed link, by card, Apple Pay or Goo=
gle Pay. Card details are only ever entered on Dojo's page.
3. Failed or unpaid payments: retried on day 2, 4 and 7, with an email each t=
ime and a fresh payment link. After that the subscription is suspended, and t=
he venue's tills pause after a 48-hour grace period. They come back on as soo=
n as the payment is captured.
4. Status: we only treat Captured as paid. The webhook names the payment inte=
nt, and we always re-read its status from the API before acting. Every POST c=
arries an idempotency key.
5. Refunds: full or partial, through the API, from our admin console. Each on=
e is recorded with who made it.
6. Sandbox checks done: payment intents created and read back, a setup intent=
 created (Unscheduled), and a refund before capture refused as expected.

Sign-up page: https://vesopaepos.com/trial (sandbox; no real money moves). Ha=
rdware: https://vesopaepos.com/hardware

WHAT WE ARE ASKING FOR
1. Live API access for Vesopa Software Ltd, so we can take subscription payme=
nts for Vesopa EPOS on our own merchant account. Please tell us what you need=
 from us for the review and onboarding.
2. Certification of this integration. We are happy to run any test script you=
 use, as we did for the menu checkout.
3. Recurring card-on-file: setup intents are single-use, so today each renewa=
l is a payment link. Can recurring merchant-initiated payments be enabled for=
 our account, or which Dojo product do you recommend for subscriptions, so re=
newals can be charged automatically with the customer's consent?
4. The sandbox checkout page: today pay.dojo.tech/checkout/pi_sandbox_... sho=
wed "upstream connect error or disconnect/reset before headers" on reload, an=
d the card fields did not load. Is this a known sandbox issue?

We would be glad to go through it on a short call whenever suits you. Just re=
ply with a time, or call me on +44 7848 494341.

Many thanks for your help.

Kind regards,
Muzahid Islam
Vesopa Developer, Vesopa Software Ltd
muzahid@vesopa.com | +44 7848 494341

On behalf of Meirion Davies, Director
Vesopa Software Ltd and Vesopa Ltd
info@vesopasoftware.com | info@vesopa.com

